o}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-19T20:20:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-19T20:24:08Z","body":"@FireDasher \r\n> No, Baking CSG does not solve the problem for me. I want it to use primitive collision. I guess I could instead make this a GDExtension on the asset store, but I think it makes more sense as a core feature.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure I understand, if you just want to use primitive collision then surely the default collision on CSG would be fine no? It shouldn't be any different from a normal box collision unless you start applying boolean operations? \r\nAccording to the docs for CSG it specifically mentions that creation of CSG nodes is what has a cost, as well as manipulating children inside the CSG node during runtime (does not mention moving the parent, so having a CSG moving platform seems to be fine?). \r\nMaybe this piece of documentation isn't fully correct, but from what I'm gathering CSG should be more than serviceable in your case. \r\n\r\nThe main use case I suppose this would be useful in is easy spawning of these primitives, but surely you'd have a Scene for such a thing for script/material/etc behavior reasons..","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5017239896/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5018144563","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121541#issuecomment-5018144563","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121541","id":5018144563,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKxrPMw","user":{"login":"FireDasher","id":150294350,"node_id":"U_kgDOCPVPTg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/150294350?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/FireDasher","html_url":"https://github.com/FireDasher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FireDasher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FireDasher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FireDasher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FireDasher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FireDasher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FireDasher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FireDasher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FireDasher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FireDasher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-20T02:07:11Z","updated_at":"2026-07-20T02:08:26Z","body":"> I'm not sure I understand, if you just want to use primitive collision then surely the default collision on CSG would be fine no? It shouldn't be any different from a normal box collision unless you start applying boolean operations?\r\n\r\nNo, if you baked a CSG box without any children you would see it still generates an ArrayMesh and a ConcavePolygonShape3D instead of a BoxMesh and a BoxShape3D. You can also see in the source code the collision shape is always a ConcavePolygonShape3D","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5018144563/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]